git history, no build output, no docs directory, and no other project file from which the checklist or its required file could be reconstructed. The workspace contains no project files at all.\n4. **Compounding effect.** The two absences are independent: fixing one does not fix the other. Both would need to be restored (checklist restored from its source of truth, required file regenerated or fetched) before the original checklist could be executed end to end.\n\n### Bottom line\n\nThe original checklist is blocked at its very first dependency: it cannot be loaded. Combined with the teammate-reported missing required file, the release process has **two confirmed blockers** with no in-workspace recovery path.\n\n### Recommendation for the next step\n\nWhen proposing the revised checklist (the next step), the workable options are: reconstruct a checklist that only depends on the single file actually present (`.gitignore`), restoring the missing required file from its upstream source if one exists, or dropping the missing-file item from the checklist with an explicit note. Tell me which you prefer, or I can draft a revised checklist around what is present and flag the missing items explicitly."